{+  Split the fibre of each binary outcome into bit and triple answers.+}
{+  Rearranging gives the second identity, and subtracting the two outcomes+}
{+  gives the observable identity.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: wrong-form bounds]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-wrong-form-bounds}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.msWrongFormEffect_bounds}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_wrong_form_norm_sq_A}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_wrong_form_norm_sq_B}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-wrong-form-effect, def:tensor-product-value}+}
{+  For every Magic Square measurement $M$, $0\le R(M)\le I$.+}
{+  If $\eps\in\mathbb R$ and $\mathcal S$ has value at least $1-\eps$,+}
{+  then at every cell $j$,+}
{+  \[+}
{+    \|(R_{A,j}\ot I)\psi\|^2\le36\eps,\qquad+}
{+    \|(I\ot R_{B,j})\psi\|^2\le36\eps.+}
{+  \]+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-game, def:ms-wrong-form-effect, def:tensor-product-value}+}
{+  The wrong-form effect is an effect of a binary postprocessing, hence a+}
{+  positive contraction. Each cell occurs in a tested incidence of weight+}
{+  $1/36$, where a triple answer on the variable side is rejected. Thus its+}
{+  expectation is at most $36\eps$; the squared-action bounds follow from+}
{+  $R^2\le R$ on either tensor factor.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: tested incidences on the original state]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-original-incidence-estimates}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_original_cell_distance_forward}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_original_cell_distance_reverse}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_original_variable_close_constraint_A}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_original_variable_close_constraint_B}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-prescribed-distances, def:ms-variable-agreement, def:tensor-product-value}+}
{+  Suppose $\eps\in\mathbb R$ and $\mathcal S$ has value at least+}
{+  $1-\eps$. For every constraint $i$ and position $k$, put $j=c(i,k)$.+}
{+  Then the completed effects satisfy+}
{+  \begin{align*}+}
{+    \sum_b\|(C^A_{i,k,b}\ot I-I\ot\hat B_{j,b})\psi\|^2&\le72\eps,\\+}
{+    \sum_b\|(\hat A_{j,b}\ot I-I\ot C^B_{i,k,b})\psi\|^2&\le72\eps.+}
{+  \end{align*}+}
{+  Here $\hat A_{j,b}=\hat A^{\mathsf{Variable}_j}_b$ and similarly for Bob.+}
{+  If also $\eps\ge0$, write $V^A_j=\hat A_{j,0}-\hat A_{j,1}$ and+}
{+  $H^A_{i,k}=C^A_{i,k,0}-C^A_{i,k,1}$, and define $V^B,H^B$ similarly.+}
{+  The corresponding observable estimates are+}
{+  \begin{align*}+}
{+    \|(V^A_j\ot I-I\ot H^B_{i,k})\psi\|&\le12\sqrt\eps,\\+}
{+    \|(I\ot V^B_j-H^A_{i,k}\ot I)\psi\|&\le12\sqrt\eps.+}
{+  \end{align*}+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-game, def:tensor-product-value, thm:ms-squared-vector-estimates}+}
{+  A mismatch of the completed bits is rejected on the corresponding+}
{+  incidence, so its mass is at most $36\eps$ in either orientation.+}
{+  The squared distance between two measurements placed on opposite factors+}
{+  is at most twice their mismatch mass. The binary-difference estimate+}
{+  of Theorem~\ref{thm:ms-squared-vector-estimates} then gives squared+}
{+  observable error at most $144\eps$.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{definition}[The one-way swap isometries]+}
{+  \label{def:ms-one-way-swap}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.msAliceOneWaySwapIsometry}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{thm:naimark, def:ms-prescribed-distances, lem:ms-rigidity-support-two-qubit-swap}+}
{+  On the questionwise Naimark dilation of $\mathcal S$, write $\psi'$ for+}
{+  the state and $H'^A_{i,k},V'^B_j$ for the completed constraint and variable+}
{+  reflections. Alice's one-way isometry $U_A$ is the two-qubit controlled+}
{+  swap built from the ordered pairs+}
{+  $(H'^A_{1,1},H'^A_{2,2})$ and $(H'^A_{1,2},H'^A_{2,1})$.+}
{+  Bob's isometry $U_B$ is the already defined controlled swap from+}
{+  $(V'^B_1,V'^B_5)$ and $(V'^B_2,V'^B_4)$.+}
{+  Explicitly, for either player's ordered list $(X_1,Z_1,X_2,Z_2)$,+}
{+  the component of the image of $v$ at register label+}
{+  $e\in\F_2^{\{0,1\}}$ is+}
{+  $X_2^{e(1)}P^{Z_2}_{e(1)}X_1^{e(0)}P^{Z_1}_{e(0)}v$,+}
{+  where $P^Z_b=(I+(-1)^bZ)/2$.+}
{+  Each auxiliary space here is that player's dilated local space.+}
{+\end{definition}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: Alice's constraint reflections]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-one-way-constraint-relations}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.msCellObsA_first_pair_anticommute}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.msCellObsA_comm_of_shared_constraint}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-one-way-swap, def:tensor-product-value}+}
{+  Let $\eps\in\mathbb R$ and suppose $\mathcal S$ has value at least+}
{+  $1-\eps$. Alice's dilated constraint reflections obey+}
{+  \[+}
{+    \|((H'^A_{1,1}H'^A_{2,2}+H'^A_{2,2}H'^A_{1,1})\ot I)\psi'\|+}
{+      \le672\sqrt\eps.+}
{+  \]+}
{+  More generally, for any constraints $I,J,i$ and positions $k,l,p,q$+}
{+  with $c(I,k)=c(i,p)$ and $c(J,l)=c(i,q)$,+}
{+  \[+}
{+    \|((H'^A_{I,k}H'^A_{J,l}-H'^A_{J,l}H'^A_{I,k})\ot I)\psi'\|+}
{+      \le144\sqrt\eps.+}
{+  \]+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-game, lem:ms-rigidity-support-second-pair,+}
{+    lem:ms-rigidity-support-marginals}+}
{+  Tested incidence agreement transfers each ordered product to the reversed+}
{+  product of Bob's variables at cost $24\sqrt\eps$. Transfer Bob's+}
{+  $624\sqrt\eps$ first-pair anticommutator in both directions. For the+}
{+  second assertion use his $96\sqrt\eps$ commutator for cells sharing+}
{+  constraint $i$, again with two product transfers.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: the specified dilated state extraction]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-one-way-dilated-state}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_one_way_dilated_state_estimate}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-one-way-swap, def:tensor-product-value, def:EPR}+}
{+  For every $\eps\in\mathbb R$ and strategy of value at least $1-\eps$,+}
{+  there is a unit vector $r$ in the tensor product of the two dilated local+}
{+  spaces such that the specified isometries satisfy+}
{+  \[+}
{+    \|(U_A\ot U_B)\psi'-\Theta(r)\|\le155904\sqrt\eps.+}
{+  \]+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{thm:ms-one-way-constraint-relations, lem:ms-rigidity-support-second-pair,+}
{+    lem:ms-rigidity-support-joint-state, def:ms-game}+}
{+  Every cross-player comparison is a tested incidence. The preceding+}
{+  relations and the second-pair estimates bound all hypotheses of the+}
{+  joint state estimate by $672\sqrt\eps$. That estimate gives a residual+}
{+  at distance $116\cdot672\sqrt\eps$; normalizing it doubles the bound.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: Bob's one-way effect transport]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-one-way-effect-transport}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.norm_ms_one_way_effect_defect_B}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-one-way-swap, def:ms-prescribed-distances}+}
{+  For every strategy, Pauli kind $W$, and $b\in\F_2$, let+}
{+  $F^B_{W,b}=(I+(-1)^b V'^B_{j_W})/2$. With $U=U_A\ot U_B$,+}
{+  \[+}
{+    \|P^{W,B}_b U\psi'-U(I\ot F^B_{W,b})\psi'\|+}
{+      \le\|(I\ot(V'^B_1V'^B_5+V'^B_5V'^B_1))\psi'\|.+}
{+  \]+}
{+  No value bound is assumed.+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{lem:ms-rigidity-support-marginals, lem:ms-rigidity-support-intertwine}+}
{+  The phase transport is exact. The shift transport has squared Gram+}
{+  operator equal to half that of the first-pair anticommutator, and passing+}
{+  to a spectral effect gives a further factor $1/4$. Tensoring with+}
{+  Alice's specified isometry preserves the squared norm.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: Bob's dilated effect distance]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-one-way-dilated-effects}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.MagicSquareRigidity.ms_one_way_dilated_operator_distance_B}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-one-way-swap, def:ms-prescribed-distances, def:tensor-product-value}+}
{+  Let $\eps\in\mathbb R$, let $\mathcal S$ have value at least+}
{+  $1-\eps$, and let $r$ be any vector in the tensor product of the dilated+}
{+  local spaces. Assume+}
{+  $\|(U_A\ot U_B)\psi'-\Theta(r)\|\le155904\sqrt\eps$.+}
{+  For each $W\in\{X,Z\}$, the completed effects+}
{+  $F^B_{W,b}$ of the dilated variable measurement satisfy+}
{+  \[+}
{+    \sum_b\|((I\ot U_B F^B_{W,b}U_B^\dagger)-P^{W,B}_b)\Theta(r)\|^2+}
{+      \le2(312432\sqrt\eps)^2.+}
{+  \]+}
{+  Normalization of $r$ is not required.+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{thm:ms-one-way-effect-transport, lem:ms-rigidity-support-marginals,+}
{+    lem:ms-rigidity-support-transfer}+}
{+  The anticommutator norm is at most $624\sqrt\eps$. Moving two+}
{+  contractions to the ideal vector costs $2\cdot155904\sqrt\eps$.+}
{+  Square the resulting $312432\sqrt\eps$ bound and sum over both bits.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: state and Bob variable extraction]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-one-way-variable-extraction}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_ms_one_way_rigidity}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-prescribed-distances, def:tensor-product-value}+}
{+  For every $\eps\ge0$ and strategy of value at least $1-\eps$, there+}
{+  is an extraction witness $w$ such that+}
{+  \[+}
{+    s_w\le155904\sqrt\eps,\qquad+}
{+    d_{B,j_W}(W)\le2\cdot10^{12}\eps\quad(W\in\{X,Z\}).+}
{+  \]+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{thm:ms-one-way-dilated-state, thm:ms-one-way-dilated-effects,+}
{+    thm:naimark, lem:ms-variable-agreement-support}+}
{+  Compose $U_A,U_B$ with the Naimark embeddings and use the unit vector+}
{+  from Theorem~\ref{thm:ms-one-way-dilated-state}. The state norm is+}
{+  unchanged. Compression and leakage bound the completed effect distance+}
{+  by $3\cdot2(312432\sqrt\eps)^2+216\eps+24(155904\sqrt\eps)^2$,+}
{+  which is at most $2\cdot10^{12}\eps$.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: ideal effects and cross-player transfer]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-ideal-measurement-transfer}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.idealMsState_pauli_actions_eq}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.ms_ideal_measurement_transfer}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-prescribed-distances}+}
{+  For any finite-dimensional auxiliary spaces, any auxiliary vector $r$+}
{+  (not necessarily unit), any $W\in\{X,Z\}$, and any $b\in\F_2$,+}
{+  $P^{W,A}_b\Theta(r)=P^{W,B}_b\Theta(r)$.+}
{+  Now fix a strategy, an extraction witness $w$, binary POVMs $E_b,F_b$+}
{+  on its respective local spaces, a Pauli kind $W$, and $s\in\mathbb R$+}
{+  with $s_w\le s$. Then+}
{+  \begin{align*}+}
{+    \sum_b\|((\widetilde E_b\ot I)-P^{W,A}_b)\Theta(r)\|^2+}
{+      &\le24s^2+3\sum_b\|(E_b\ot I-I\ot F_b)\psi\|^2\\+}
{+      &\quad+3\sum_b\|((I\ot\widetilde F_b)-P^{W,B}_b)\Theta(r)\|^2.+}
{+  \end{align*}+}
{+\end{theorem}+}
{+\begin{proof}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:EPR, def:ms-prescribed-distances}+}
{+  Both Pauli effects are real symmetric, so their actions on opposite+}
{+  halves of the EPR state agree. Insert the transported original state+}
{+  between the two transported effects. Contractivity bounds the+}
{+  state-change term by $2s$ for each bit, isometric transport preserves+}
{+  the original comparison, and the squared three-term triangle inequality+}
{+  gives the asserted sum.+}
{+\end{proof}+}

{+\begin{theorem}[Formalization support: completed variable agreement transfer]+}
{+  \label{thm:ms-variable-distance-transfer}+}
{+  \lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.ms_variable_distance_le_agreement}+}
{+  \leanok+}
{+  \uses{def:ms-prescribed-distances, def:ms-variable-agreement}+}
{+  For every strategy, extraction witness $w$, cell $j$, Pauli kind $W$,+}
{+  and real $s$ with $s_w\le s$,+}
